{"tool_name":"reactpred","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"ReactPRED","home":"https://sourceforge.net/projects/reactpred/","license":"Unlicense","summary":"Tool to predict and analyze biochemical reactions.","addition_date":"2019-08-04T11:04:46Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T21:06:24.513506Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool","Desktop application"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:ReactPRED","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"anirban.b@samsung.com","name":"Anirban Bhaduri","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]},{"email":"ty76.kim@samsung.com","name":"Tae Yong Kim","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"https://sourceforge.net/projects/reactpred/files/ReadME.txt/download"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Enrichment analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3501"},{"term":"Pathway or network analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2497"}]}],"maturity":"Mature","name":"ReactPRED","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Ruta","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/btw491","metadata":{"abstract":"Motivation: Biochemical pathways engineering is often used to synthesize or degrade target chemicals. In silico screening of the biochemical transformation space allows predicting feasible reactions, constituting these pathways. Current enabling tools are customized to predict reactions based on pre-defined biochemical transformations or reaction rule sets. Reaction rule sets are usually curated manually and tailored to specific applications. They are not exhaustive. In addition, current systems are incapable of regulating and refining data with an aim to tune specificity and sensitivity. A robust and flexible tool that allows automated reaction rule set creation along with regulated pathway prediction and analyses is a need. ReactPRED aims to address the same. Results: ReactPRED is an open source flexible and customizable tool enabling users to predict biochemical reactions and pathways. The tool allows automated reaction rule creation from a user defined reaction set. Additionally, reaction rule degree and rule tolerance features allow refinement of predicted data. It is available as a flexible graphical user interface and a console application.","authors":[{"name":"Bhaduri A."},{"name":"Giri V."},{"name":"Kim T.Y."},{"name":"Park J.H."},{"name":"Sivakumar T.V."}],"citationCount":29,"date":"2016-11-15T00:00:00Z","journal":"Bioinformatics","title":"ReactPRED: A tool to predict and analyze biochemical reactions"},"pmid":"27485447","type":["Benchmarking study"]}],"topic":[{"term":"Biochemistry","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3292"},{"term":"Literature and language","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3068"},{"term":"Molecular interactions, pathways and networks","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0602"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"ReactPRED","home":"https://bio.tools/ReactPRED","license":"Unlicense","summary":"Tool to predict and analyze biochemical reactions.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:reactpred/app/sourceforge.net","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"source_packages":true,"sourcecode":{}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"documentation":{"general":true},"license":{"open_source":true,"osi":false},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":11,"citations":[{"count":1,"year":"2017"},{"count":1,"year":"2018"},{"count":1,"year":"2019"},{"count":1,"year":"2020"},{"count":1,"year":"2022"},{"count":2,"year":"2023"},{"count":4,"year":"2021"}],"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/btw491","pmid":"27485447","ref_count":0,"refs":[],"title":"ReactPRED: a tool to predict and analyze biochemical reactions.","year":2016}]}],"sum